 "_readme": "Gremlish: a simple letter-substitution cipher. 'key' maps each letter to a glyph shape from 'glyphs'. TO SWAP THE KEY: reorder which shape each letter points to in 'key' (every shape used once), save, redeploy. Every note in house-notes.json re-renders from this file. Shapes are drawn in a unit box (x,y 0..1, y down): l=line x1,y1,x2,y2; p=polyline [points], closed; c=circle cx,cy,r; a=arc cx,cy,r,startDeg,endDeg (0=east, clockwise); d=dot x,y. These shapes come from the Gremlish alphabet already used on the painted plaques (Moth may redraw them). NOTE: the plaques in the Burrow and Corridor are static SVGs drawn with the CURRENT key, so after a swap they no longer match the notes until they're redrawn.",
